WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.320
Eight runners crouch in their lanes.

2
00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:03.900
The gun fires.

3
00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:07.040
At the finish stands
an empty podium: first,

4
00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:08.650
second and third.

5
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:10.220
No ties allowed.

6
00:00:10.270 --> 00:00:13.870
Runner five wins, then
runners two and seven.

7
00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:17.330
Run it again, and the podium
could look completely different.

8
00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:19.810
How many different podiums are possible?

9
00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:21.160
Is it eight cubed?

10
00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:21.920
Fewer?

11
00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:22.900
More?

12
00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:26.330
In this mission, you'll use
the multiplication principle:

13
00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:31.220
fill the places one at a time, and
multiply the number of ways at each stage.

14
00:00:31.270 --> 00:00:34.580
And you'll learn when order
matters, a permutation,

15
00:00:34.630 --> 00:00:37.000
and when it doesn't, a combination.

16
00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:41.160
Your mission: work out how many
ways eight runners can finish first,

17
00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:42.610
second and third.
